cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Spillover, please cite the software as below. To cite one claim, use the
  "Copy citation" or "BibTeX" button on its page, which names the exact claim version,
  scoring rules and commit.
title: "Spillover: an open ledger that tests how news spills over into markets"
type: software
# Replace with your real name if you want it cited (given-names / family-names), for example:
#   - given-names: Jane
#     family-names: Doe
#     alias: McMuf
authors:
  - name: McMuf
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24409543"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24409543"
    description: "Zenodo archive of release v0.1.0a0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/McMuf/Spillover"
url: "https://mcmuf.github.io/Spillover/"
abstract: >-
  Spillover registers claims about how kinds of news move markets, freezes and
  timestamps a prediction for every new qualifying event before its outcome is known,
  and grades the claims with a public event-study method (market model, cumulative
  abnormal returns, Student t-intervals checked by simulation, fixed stopping and
  false-discovery-rate control).
keywords:
  - event study
  - pre-registration
  - financial markets
  - news
  - open science
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0a0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
